# Thekra phone app — settings
#
# Copy this file to mobile/.env and fill it in:   cp .env.example .env
# mobile/.env is ignored by git. Expo reads it when it bundles the app (npx expo start,
# npx expo run:ios, EAS builds), so restart Metro after changing it.
#
# Only EXPO_PUBLIC_* values reach the app, and everything here ends up INSIDE the app that
# people install: never put a secret (API keys, Stripe, SMS) here. Those live on the server
# (see the root .env.example).
#
# A line left empty counts as not set.

# The Thekra server the app talks to, without a trailing slash.
#   iOS Simulator on this Mac:     http://localhost:8787
#   A real phone on the same Wi-Fi: http://<this Mac's LAN address>:8787
#   Staging / production:          https://<your domain>
# Not set: a development build uses http://localhost:8787; a release build has no server
# and logs that it was built without one.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=
